# Byte-stability for SHA-256-pinned governance documents.
#
# Run-control authorization records pin their governing documents by SHA-256 of
# the documents' exact bytes. A digest is only meaningful if those bytes are
# identical on every platform. Without `-text`, Git's end-of-line conversion
# rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout wherever core.autocrlf is enabled (the
# default on Windows, including GitHub's windows-latest runners), which changes
# the file's on-disk bytes and therefore silently invalidates every digest
# computed over them.
#
# `-text` disables that conversion, so these files are checked out byte-for-byte
# as committed. Any document referenced by a `*_sha256` field in an
# authorization record MUST be listed here.
docs/experiments/STAGE-1-AUTEUR-POST-REMEDIATION-PREPARATION.md -text
docs/experiments/GATE-D-STALE-DIAGNOSIS-CHECKLIST.md -text

# The run-control tree carries its own `* -text`; this is defence in depth so a
# deleted or moved nested .gitattributes cannot silently reintroduce the bug.
experiments/run-control/** -text

# Campaign packages are digest-bound (policy_digest / configuration_id and
# the *_sha256 sidecar); their bytes must be identical on every platform.
experiments/campaigns/EXP-0002-stage1-auteur-coding-agent-pilot/** -text
